export anchor NightLightStyle:
    number: 376
    screen: SmartHome
    name: Night light
    idea: A bedside screen in warm low amber on near black, one narrow quiet column with a large clock and old style serif text, dim enough for a dark bedroom yet every word still clears AA.
    base: dark
    palette:
        page: #0c0805, page and style sheet ground
        glow: #140d08, faint top glow behind the clock
        rule: #2e1f14, hairline rules between rows
        ink: #dcae80, body text, 9 to 1 on page
        soft: #a8805c, labels, italics and notes, 5.6 to 1
        ember: #f0a560, the clock, active scene, primary button and focus
        onEmber: #1a0d03, text on ember
        emberDeep: #3a2210, the alert band
        alert: #f3b780, alert text on emberDeep
    type:
        Old style serif for text, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype,
        Palatino, Book Antiqua, Georgia, base 17px at 1.6. The clock is
        112px at 400 in ember with old style figures, the bedroom line 24px,
        room names 20px, notes 15px italic. Small labels and buttons use
        system-ui at 12px, 600, caps with 0.18em tracking.
    layout:
        One quiet centred column 680px wide on a near black brown page with
        a faint warm radial glow at the top. A small caps line names
        Brightwork Home and Bedtime view. A huge ember clock shows the time,
        with an italic line Saturday evening, Movie is playing. A ruled
        Bedroom block comes first, saying 19.0 degrees and cooling for
        sleep, with a clock line that heating steps down to 18 at bedtime. A
        deep ember alert band follows with an exclamation mark, the garage
        sentence and an ember pill Close now. Around the house lists the
        other four rooms as rows with dotted leaders from the name to the
        value and an italic note with a thin icon below. Today's energy
        shows three figures split by thin left rules, then a dim curve of
        dots, brighter ember dots for the evening, captioned midnight,
        busiest at seven and now. Scenes are outlined pills with Movie in
        ember and a small on mark. A closing italic hint explains Good
        night. At phone width the clock drops to 84px.
    spacing: An 8px unit with generous 40 to 48px gaps between sections and 14px row padding.
    density: Very low. One fact per line, bedroom first.
    corners: Square rows, a 4px alert band, full pills for buttons and scenes.
    borders: 1px #2e1f14 rules only, and dotted #4a3322 leaders between a room and its value.
    shadows: None. A faint radial glow behind the clock instead.
    icons: Thin 1.3 stroke line icons at 18px, always beside a full sentence.
    focus: A 2px dashed ember outline offset 4px, dashed so it reads apart from the solid rules.
    tone: Hushed sentences, such as Around the house and Heating steps down to 18.
